.TH LZHAM 1 "September 2026" "LZHAM 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lzham \- high-ratio LZ compression utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lzham
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE...\fR]
.br
.B lzham
.B c
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
.br
.B lzham
.B d
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR \fIOUTPUT\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lzham
is a high-ratio lossless data compression tool created by Richard Geldreich.
It achieves high compression ratios comparable to LZMA while providing faster
decompression speeds and support for dictionaries up to 512 MB.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-stdout
Write output on standard output; keep original files unchanged.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompress
Decompress files.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test archive integrity using embedded Adler-32 checksums.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force overwrite of output files without prompting.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep (do not delete) input files.
.TP
.BI \-m level
Set compression level from 0 (fastest) to 4 (uber). Default is 2.
.TP
.BI \-d dict
Set log2 dictionary size from 15 (32 KB) to 29 (512 MB). Default is 26 (64 MB).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential messages.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help.
.SH AUTHORS
Written by Richard Geldreich, Jr.
Packaged for Trinity Desktop Environment (TDE) / TdeZip.
